speechtext:
May I reply, with the permission of the hon. member for Laurier. This is the part to which we had an amendment, and it reads:
(a) "municipal sewerage corporation" means a corporation established for the purpose of constructing and operating facilities for the collection and treatment of sewage from one or more municipalities;
I can assure the hon. member that that is what it means, and that is what it says. Under no circumstances would there be any private corporation which could possibly be a municipal sewerage corporation. I can assure him that there will be no grants made by us to any private corporations. These grants will be made to municipalities or to municipal sewerage corporations created by municipalities. This is a very good question but I would have preferred to have the hon. member ask it rather than take the time of the house with an unnecessary amendment.
